Instances of multiple sequence alignment, in the FASTA format (.tfa).

balibase/  the files of msa/BAliBASE of
           https://github.com/jinnaiyuu/combinatorial_instances, sequences
           of BAliBASE 3.0 (J. D. Thompson, P. Koehl, R. Ripp and O. Poch,
           "BAliBASE 3.0: latest developments of the multiple sequence
           alignment benchmark", Proteins 61, 2005), as selected there.
easy/      the files of BAliBASE/easy of
           https://github.com/jinnaiyuu/Hash-Distributed-Astar, short
           sequences cut from the same benchmark.
papers/    the 15 files .tfa of BAliBASE 3.0 (directories RV11 and RV12
           of BAliBASE3.0.tar, downloaded from
           https://www.lbgi.fr/balibase/BalibaseDownload/BAliBASE_R1-5.tar.gz)
           used by Y. Kobayashi, A. Kishimoto and O. Watanabe, IJCAI 2011
           (BB12003, BB12022, BB12023, BB12032, BB12036, BBS11026,
           BBS11037, BBS12005, BBS12010, BBS12023, BBS12032) and by
           Y. Jinnai and A. Fukunaga, JAIR 60, 2017, section 4.1.3
           (BB12021, BB12022, BB12036, BBS11010, BBS11026, BBS11035,
           BBS11037, BBS12016, BBS12023, BBS12032); BBS11035 is also in
           balibase/. The archive states no license; its README names
           J. D. Thompson as the contact.

